# Production mutation boundary

Agent sessions must not mutate Production outside `requireOwnerProductionApply`.

Allowed Production database work from an agent:

- Read-only diagnostics (`pnpm db:prod:audit`, `pnpm dbs`, MCP `list_migrations`, MCP `execute_sql` with SELECT only).
- Canonical owner workflows that still fail closed here because `CELEBRA_AGENT_CONTEXT` is set.

Forbidden from an agent, even with Production credentials in the environment:

- Canonical Production `--apply` (`pnpm prod:apply -- --apply`, `db:migrate -- --target production --apply`, `invitation:release -- --targets production --apply`, `db:prod:patch --apply`).
- Supabase MCP `apply_migration`, mutating `execute_sql`, `deploy_edge_function`, or branch mutation tools targeting Production.
- Raw `supabase db push`, `supabase migration up`, `supabase db reset`, or `psql` writes against Production.
- Invoking `executeSupabasePush` / `executePsqlAtomicPending` / `apply-migrations.ts` against Production.

Owner apply: `pnpm prod:apply` from an interactive owner terminal (not this agent).
Preview remains agent-operable under its existing authorization policy.
